<title>USA: EMU criteria to be applied in &quot;good faith&quot; - Brittan.</title>
<headline>EMU criteria to be applied in &quot;good faith&quot; - Brittan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union Trade Commissioner Leon Brittan said the EU will interpret &quot;in good faith&quot; the criteria for joining a proposed single European currency in 1999.</p>
<p>Responding to a question at the European-American Chamber of Commerce, Brittan noted that several of the criteria are written to allow for progress toward budgetary benchmarks.  </p>
<p>&quot;That is not fudging. That is applying the criteria. It will be an application of the criteria in good faith,&quot; said Brittan.</p>
<p>Brittan added that the financial markets will be the judge of whether or not those criteria will be applied in good faith.</p>
<p>-- Chris Stetkiewicz, 212-859-1664</p>
</text>
